{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>In fire.</b> [By way of metaphor] for burning anger, and the meaning is destructive decrees, suddenly, in an instant." "<b>And like a stormwind, His chariots.</b> In the manner of a king." "<b>To render in fury.</b> When there is a construct of ḥaron joined with mem it is for praise, and with bet for blame."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:14.099237791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}